00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:26.800
Investors should watch how index rebalancing flows

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:28.720
interact with today's volatility

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:31.740
into the June 22 effective date.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.220
With volatility this elevated,

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:36.420
one strategy is already positioning

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.260
ahead of mechanical index flows.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:39.140
Here's how.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:43.700
Index reconstitution creates measurable short term price pressure

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:45.640
on both additions and deletions

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:48.680
because passive funds must rebalance holdings

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:50.460
on or before the effective date.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:55.780
Today's announcement that Marvel and Flex will join the S&amp;P 500

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:58.620
while pool corp and Campbell's are removed

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:02.060
gives active investors a narrow window to front run

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:03.660
the mechanical buying and selling.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.160
The strategy is to screen for names

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:09.080
with high passive ownership that are also additions.

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:12.160
Size positions small enough that the expected

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:16.420
3 to 8% inclusion pop still clears transaction costs.

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:19.800
Implementation is straightforward on any platform

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:21.440
that offers pre-market trading.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:25.980
Place limit orders the Friday before the June 22 effective date

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:29.300
and exit once the rebalancing volumes of sides.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:34.160
Historically this works best when broader market volatility is low.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.760
The current geopolitical backdrop raises the risk

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:40.140
that the move is swamped by macro flows.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.580
Risk is therefore managed by keeping the position

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:45.760
under 2% of portfolio value

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:48.200
and using the 20-day volume average

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.680
as a confirmation filter before entry.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:54.140
While we wait for the right volume confirmed setups

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.640
let's quickly cover the options basics

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.600
that can generate income in the meantime.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:02.920
Imagine you own 100 shares of Royal Bank of Canada

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:06.840
trading at $145 and you want extra income

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.820
while you hold through a quiet summer.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:13.080
You sell one covered call with a $150 strike

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:14.760
expiring in 30 days

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.400
and collect a $2.10 premium.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:22.080
Your effective sale price becomes $152.10

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:23.800
if the stock is called away.

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:27.380
That premium is compensation for giving someone else

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:29.920
the right to buy your shares at $150.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:33.640
A call gives the buyer the right to purchase at the strike.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:36.420
A put gives the buyer the right to sell at the strike.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:40.480
The two Greeks that matter most for covered call writers are Delta

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:43.340
how much the option price moves with the stock

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:47.120
and Theta how much value the option loses each day

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.640
as expiration approaches.

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:52.200
Most retail investors never open the options chain

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:56.680
to see that the $150 call is only $2.10

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:59.780
because they assume options are only for speculation.

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:04.380
The biggest mistake with covered calls is selling naked calls

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.020
on stock you do not own.

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:09.260
Instead always start with the covered variety

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:12.000
on shares already sitting in your TFSA

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.360
so the maximum loss remains the decline in the underlying shares

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:18.240
minus the premium received.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:21.440
That same discipline of waiting for aligned factors

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:24.260
shows up in today's practice investment decision.

